{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0732"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge sport-games/games","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/zz-r2-sport-games__games.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",820],["+","Mario's own moves were kept just as simple. Most players believe that he smashes the brick blocks above him by jumping into them head first, but Nintendo describes it differently: the original instruction booklet speaks of Mario punching through bricks, and Nintendo's own text in \"Mario Party 9\" tells players to break the blocks with your fist and not your head.\n\n"],["=",369]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",764],["+","Marios eigene Bewegungen blieben ebenso einfach. Die meisten Spieler glauben, dass er die Ziegelblöcke über sich mit dem Kopf zertrümmert, wenn er dagegen springt, doch Nintendo beschreibt es anders: Die Original-Spielanleitung spricht davon, dass Mario die Steine durchschlägt, und Nintendos eigener Text in „Mario Party 9“ fordert dazu auf, die Blöcke mit der Faust und nicht mit dem Kopf zu zerschlagen.\n\n"],["=",349]]}]},
